4. INTERVENTIONS   interchange = everything named at the site is copied from another input's run (need 90%). Then tests that make states no input produces (need 50% of the cases where the decision changed): partial = one variable is copied while the site's other variables stay; edit = a random half of the coordinates of everything named at the site are copied. Where both are run, it is enough that all partial tests pass OR the edit passes. right = the construction predicted the network's new decision (all cases / cases where the decision changed).  controls: the same swap in a random subspace; guessing 'no change'; guessing the source input's output; attribution patching (a first-order estimate computed on the network itself)
